  "note": "From the OpenStreetMap export (the corridor's tracks and platforms, 8 October 2026), 1.25 times real across the line like the tracks: bays 1 to 12 run back from the buffer stops at about u = 40, platform 5 (the stopper, turning round) and 6 (the expresses) on the corridor, the rest laid parallel to it as islands 2/3, 4/5, 6/7, 8/9 and the single platforms 1, 10, 11 and 12, their tracks fanning into the throat. The bays really splay; they're drawn parallel. Platforms 13 and 14, on the line to Oxford Road, aren't drawn yet. Trains stop 35 m short of the station's point so the longest unit clears the buffers. Positive v is east (London Road side). Photos: the great glazed arched train shed over the bays, and canopies on columns along the platforms that run out beyond it. It starts as a halt: a strip of the island along platform 5 with lamps. The concourse (with room for barriers and the food hall), then the train shed and the other bays, build it up; the tracks are scenery.",
